<meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"></head><body><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;
font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><font color="#000000">Welcome to the lower camp!
Step inside and reflect on everything you have learned in the design process before
moving on to the participation phase.<o:p></o:p></font></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;
font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><font color="#000000">Find inspiration for
reflection sessions below, while on the next page, you can contribute to our
ongoing research for the further development of transdisciplinary education.<o:p></o:p></font></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><font color="#000000"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:
116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Campfire conversations:
a reflection break in the TRAIL</span></b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB"> <o:p></o:p></span></font></p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;
font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><font color="#000000">You have just
completed an important phase. Take some time to look back and reflect with your
group.<o:p></o:p></font></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><font color="#000000"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:
116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Sharing Circle</span></b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"> <o:p></o:p></span></font></p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;
font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><font color="#000000">Share your
experiences and feelings with each other in the open setting of a sharing
circle: an open setting for all project participants to share their experiences
and feelings with the group. For a productive and safe group conversation, it
is important that a moderator is well-prepared and follows guidelines. You can
find these guidelines in <a href="https://www.globallearningpartners.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/Sharing-Circle-Guidelines.pdf">this
article</a>.<o:p></o:p></font></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:
116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><font color="#000000">Discussion
canvas of collaboration<o:p></o:p></font></span></b></p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;
font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><font color="#000000">Use the <a href="https://www.wijzijnkatapult.nl/files/downloads/Tools/Tool_3-Katapult_reflectie_tool_samenwerken%20v0.4.pdf">discussion
canvas</a> from Katapult [in Dutch, English tool will follow soon] to reflect
on the collaboration and determine which aspects of the collaboration need
extra attention. Collaboration partners can first map out their own perspective
on the collaboration, and subsequently bring these visions together to form a
shared understanding of the collaboration.</font><o:p></o:p></span></p></body></html>